{"archetypes":[{"name":"shell-semantics","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The fix introduces new Bash arithmetic, subshell variable scoping, and function-scope variable declarations that interact with set -euo pipefail in non-obvious ways.","prompt_body":"Examine the new `step5_probe_prior_round_env` helper and the `run_implement_loop` entry-time block in `skills/review-and-fix/scripts/review-implement-step5-loop.sh`. Verify that all arithmetic expansions are safe under `set -euo pipefail` — in particular that `(( expr ))` with a zero result does not abort the script, and that `local var=...` with a command substitution does not suppress the exit code of the subcommand under older Bash. Check whether `prior_round_num` and `expected_env_path` are declared `local` before use or leak into the caller scope. Confirm the `|| true` guard on `flush_review_batches` is correctly positioned so a non-zero exit cannot propagate. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-isolation","focus_area":"code-robustness","weight":1,"rationale":"The new test section sources lib-implement-round-cap.sh and review-implement-step5-loop.sh at file scope and then redefines functions inside a subshell; cross-section state leakage and eval-based function renaming are fragile.","prompt_body":"Review `skills/review-and-fix/scripts/test-review-and-fix.sh` lines added in the `step5-starting-round` and `parsers` sections. Focus on whether the `eval \"$(declare -f ...)\"` rename of `count_prior_degraded_rounds` can corrupt the parsers section if both sections run sequentially (without `--section`), since the rename occurs at file scope in parsers and then the step5 section sources the same library again. Check whether the `sync` function override inside the subshell leaks back to the outer shell on any shell variant. Verify that `STEP5_LAST_CASE_DIR`, `STEP5_SYNC_MODE`, and other globals set by `step5_run_loop_case` are fully reset between cases and cannot cause false-pass from stale state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"envelope-contract","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The SKILL.md stall bullet was significantly rewritten to retain STALL_TRACKING from the envelope; the new prose also seeds ship-pr-state.sh, which is a new side-effect not present in the original bullet and not mentioned in the plan's acceptance criteria as a loop-script responsibility.","prompt_body":"Read the updated `**stall**` bullet in `skills/implement/SKILL.md` and compare it against the plan's acceptance criterion 4. The new prose instructs the orchestrator to rewrite or seed `ship-pr-state.sh` before jumping to Step 16 — check whether this is actually required by the `restore-finalize-state.sh` contract documented in `docs/run-logs.md` or `skills/implement/SKILL.md` Step 18, or whether it introduces a new obligation not backed by the downstream consumer. Also verify that the `STALL_TRACKING` retain-from-envelope instruction is self-consistent: if the envelope emits `STALL_TRACKING=false` and the orchestrator variable is also named `STALL_TRACKING`, confirm there is no naming collision with the `stall_track` local variable used inside `run_implement_loop`. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"diagnostic-line-format","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan specifies a single larch_err line with six KEY=value tokens separated by spaces; the test assertion uses grep with a regex requiring all six on one line, but the implementation emits them as positional shell arguments which may be word-split differently.","prompt_body":"Inspect the `larch_err` call added in `skills/review-and-fix/scripts/review-implement-step5-loop.sh` around the `starting-round-invalid` path: verify that the six `KEY=value` pairs are passed as a single argument (quoted string) so they land on one stderr line, not as six separate arguments that could be newline-separated depending on how `larch_err` is implemented. Then check `step5_assert_diagnostic_keys` in `skills/review-and-fix/scripts/test-review-and-fix.sh`: the grep pattern requires all six tokens on one line — confirm this matches the actual emission format. If `larch_err` internally joins its arguments with spaces, verify that spaces inside `expected_env_path` values (unlikely but possible) would not split the token. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
